The numbers that the API is given are looked at before they are used

Two calls take a number from outside and use it as it comes. A number that
nobody means to pass is then undefined behaviour instead of an answer, and
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer stops the program at it:

  src/adlmidi_opl3.cpp:149:39: runtime error: shift exponent 95 is too large
  for 32-bit type 'unsigned int'

* adl_isEmulatorAvailable() answers whether an emulator is in the build by
  shifting a bit into the word of the emulators that were built. Being asked
  about any number at all is what the function is for, so it says no to a
  number that no bit of that word could stand for, rather than shifting past
  the end of it. adl_switchEmulator() asks it first, so an emulator out of
  range is turned away there as it was.

* adl_setVolumeRangeModel() passed the number on as an ADLMIDI_VolumeModels,
  and reading a value that the enumeration does not have is undefined as well.
  libOPNMIDI, whose enumeration is shorter, shows it plainly:

    src/opnmidi_opn2.cpp:511:12: runtime error: load of value 15, which is not
    a valid value for type 'OPNMIDI_VolumeModels'

  A number that is not one of the models is taken for
  ADLMIDI_VolumeModel_AUTO, the library's own choice when nothing is chosen.

Both came from a fuzz target of ADLplug-Next that gives the real-time API what
a host and a saved project can ask of it: an emulator number and a volume model
both come out of a project, which the plugin does not write itself.

This is ADLplug-Next's own patch, applied to the submodule by
cmake/Patches.cmake when CMake configures, and it goes away once the change is
upstream.

diff --git a/src/adlmidi.cpp b/src/adlmidi.cpp
index e341f91..d7509c1 100644
--- a/src/adlmidi.cpp
+++ b/src/adlmidi.cpp
@@ -722,6 +722,9 @@ ADLMIDI_EXPORT void adl_setVolumeRangeModel(struct ADL_MIDIPlayer *device, int v
     if(!device)
         return;
 
+    if(volumeModel < 0 || volumeModel >= ADLMIDI_VolumeModel_Count)
+        volumeModel = ADLMIDI_VolumeModel_AUTO;
+
     MidiPlayer *play = GET_MIDI_PLAYER(device);
     assert(play);
     Synth &synth = *play->m_synth;
diff --git a/src/adlmidi_opl3.cpp b/src/adlmidi_opl3.cpp
index d5ed16f..ac75832 100644
--- a/src/adlmidi_opl3.cpp
+++ b/src/adlmidi_opl3.cpp
@@ -146,6 +146,8 @@ static const unsigned adl_emulatorSupport = 0
 //! Check emulator availability
 bool adl_isEmulatorAvailable(int emulator)
 {
+    if(emulator < 0 || (unsigned)emulator >= sizeof(adl_emulatorSupport) * 8)
+        return false;
     return (adl_emulatorSupport & (1u << (unsigned)emulator)) != 0;
 }
 
